### ==============================================================================
### PHASE 1: AUTHENTICATION, USERS & RBAC (Shared Core API)
### Run directly inside VS Code by clicking "Send Request" above each endpoint
### ==============================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1. SEED DATA & DEPARTMENTS
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 1.1 List All Departments (Public / Authenticated)
# @name listDepartments
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/identity/departments
Content-Type: application/json

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2. EMPLOYEE REGISTRATION & AUTHENTICATION
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 2.1 Register New Employee (Role is strictly locked to EMPLOYEE)
# @name registerEmployee
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "firstName": "John",
    "lastName": "Doe",
    "email": "john.doe@company.com",
    "password": "Password123!",
    "jobTitle": "Software Engineer",
    "phone": "+254711000111",
    "departmentId": "{{listDepartments.response.body.data[1].id}}"
}

### 2.2 Login as Registered Employee
# @name employeeLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "john.doe@company.com",
    "password": "Password123!"
}

### Store Employee Tokens
@employeeToken = {{employeeLogin.response.body.data.accessToken}}
@employeeRefreshToken = {{employeeLogin.response.body.data.refreshToken}}
@employeeUserId = {{employeeLogin.response.body.data.userId}}

### 2.3 Get Current Employee Profile & Hierarchy (/me)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/identity/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}

### 2.4 Verify RBAC: Employee Cannot Create Users (Expect HTTP 403 Forbidden)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/identity/users
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "firstName": "Hacker",
    "lastName": "Admin",
    "email": "hacker@company.com",
    "password": "Password123!",
    "roleName": "HR_ADMIN"
}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3. HR ADMINISTRATOR WORKFLOW
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 3.1 Login as Default Seeded HR Admin
# @name hrAdminLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "hr.admin@company.com",
    "password": "Admin123!"
}

### Store HR Admin Token
@adminToken = {{hrAdminLogin.response.body.data.accessToken}}

### 3.2 List All Users (HR Admin only)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/identity/users
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 3.3 HR Admin Creates a Line Manager Account
# @name createManager
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/identity/users
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "firstName": "Alice",
    "lastName": "Smith",
    "email": "alice.manager@company.com",
    "password": "Password123!",
    "roleName": "LINE_MANAGER",
    "jobTitle": "Engineering Lead",
    "phone": "+254722000222",
    "departmentId": "{{listDepartments.response.body.data[1].id}}"
}

### Store Manager ID
@managerId = {{createManager.response.body.data.id}}

### 3.4 HR Admin Assigns Line Manager to Employee
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/identity/users/{{employeeUserId}}/manager
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "managerId": "{{managerId}}"
}

### 3.5 Re-check Employee Profile (Now reflects assigned manager in reporting_hierarchy)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/identity/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 4. TOKEN ROTATION & REVOCATION (Opaque Refresh Tokens)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 4.1 Rotate Refresh Token (Generates new access token + new refresh token)
# @name refreshToken
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "refreshToken": "{{employeeRefreshToken}}"
}

### Store Rotated Token
@newRefreshToken = {{refreshToken.response.body.data.refreshToken}}

### 4.2 Logout (Revokes Refresh Token)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "refreshToken": "{{newRefreshToken}}"
}

### 4.3 Attempt Refresh with Revoked Token (Expect HTTP 401 Unauthorized)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "refreshToken": "{{newRefreshToken}}"
}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 5. RATE LIMITING (5 Failed Attempts -> 15 min Lockout)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Test 5 Failed Attempts (returns 401: "Invalid email or password")
### 6th Attempt returns 429 Too Many Requests: "Too many failed login attempts..."
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "john.doe@company.com",
    "password": "WrongPassword!"
}

### ==============================================================================
### 6. PHASE 2: ORGANIZATION HIERARCHY (REPORTING LINES)
### ==============================================================================

### 6.1 HR Admin Assigns Manager to Employee (POST /api/identity/hierarchy/assign)
# @name assignHierarchy
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/identity/hierarchy/assign
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "employeeId": "{{employeeUserId}}",
    "managerId": "{{managerId}}",
    "relationshipType": "DIRECT"
}

### 6.2 Caller's Current Manager (GET /api/identity/hierarchy/my-manager)
### IDOR-safe: Derives employee ID strictly from JWT
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/identity/hierarchy/my-manager
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}

### 6.3 Caller's Direct Reports (GET /api/identity/hierarchy/my-subordinates)
### Called by Manager -> Returns employee list
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/identity/hierarchy/my-subordinates
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}

### 6.4 HR Admin Views Any User's Direct Reports (GET /api/identity/hierarchy/{userId}/subordinates)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/identity/hierarchy/{{managerId}}/subordinates
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 6.5 Test Validation: Reject Self-Reporting (Expect HTTP 400 Bad Request)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/identity/hierarchy/assign
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "employeeId": "{{employeeUserId}}",
    "managerId": "{{employeeUserId}}"
}

### 6.6 Test Validation: Reject Assignment from Non-Admin (Expect HTTP 403 Forbidden)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/identity/hierarchy/assign
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "employeeId": "{{employeeUserId}}",
    "managerId": "{{managerId}}"
}

### ==============================================================================
### 7. PHASE 3: LEAVE POLICIES & BALANCES CATALOG
### ==============================================================================

### 7.1 List Active Leave Types (Any authenticated user)
# @name listLeaveTypes
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/leave/types
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}

### 7.2 List Active Leave Policies (Any authenticated user)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/leave/policies
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}

### 7.3 Get Current Employee's Leave Balances (/me)
### IDOR-Safe: Strictly derives identity from JWT token
# @name myBalances
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/leave/balances/me
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}

### 7.4 HR Admin: Inspect Specific Employee's Balances
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/leave/balances/user/{{employeeUserId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 7.5 HR Admin: Create Custom Leave Type (POST /api/leave/types)
# @name createLeaveType
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/leave/types
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "code": "VOLUNTEER",
    "name": "Community Volunteer Leave",
    "description": "Paid leave for participating in registered community service initiatives",
    "isPaid": true,
    "requiresAttachment": false
}

### Store Volunteer Type ID
@volunteerTypeId = {{createLeaveType.response.body.data.id}}

### 7.6 HR Admin: Create/Update Policy for Leave Type (Closes prior active policy)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/leave/policies
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "leaveTypeId": "{{volunteerTypeId}}",
    "policyName": "Volunteer Leave 2026",
    "annualAllowance": 5.0,
    "monthlyAccrualRate": 0.0,
    "maxCarryoverDays": 0.0,
    "carryoverExpiryMonths": 0,
    "effectiveYear": 2026
}

### 7.7 HR Admin: Manual Balance Adjustment (Audited via balance_transactions)
@annualBalanceId = {{myBalances.response.body.data[0].id}}

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/leave/balances/{{annualBalanceId}}/adjust
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "transactionType": "MANUAL_ADJUSTMENT",
    "amountDays": 5.0,
    "description": "Mid-year discretionary performance bonus days"
}

### 7.8 Test Validation: Employee Attempting Policy Creation (Expect HTTP 403 Forbidden)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/leave/policies
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "leaveTypeId": "{{volunteerTypeId}}",
    "policyName": "Unauthorized Policy",
    "annualAllowance": 100.0,
    "effectiveYear": 2026
}

### ==============================================================================
### PHASE 4: LEAVE REQUEST & APPROVAL STATE MACHINE
### ==============================================================================

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 8. LEAVE REQUEST SUBMISSION & EMPLOYEE ACTIONS
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 8.1 Employee Submits a Leave Request (3 working days)
### Hold vs. Deduct: pending_days increases, used_days is NOT touched.
# @name submitLeaveRequest
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/leave/requests
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "leaveTypeId": "{{listLeaveTypes.response.body.data[0].id}}",
    "startDate": "2026-10-05",
    "endDate": "2026-10-07",
    "reason": "Family vacation",
    "attachmentUrl": null
}

### Store Leave Request ID
@leaveRequestId = {{submitLeaveRequest.response.body.data.id}}

### 8.2 Get Current Employee's Leave Request History (/my-requests)
### Anti-IDOR: Identity derived strictly from authenticated JWT principal
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/leave/requests/my-requests
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}

### 8.3 Get Single Leave Request Details
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/leave/requests/{{leaveRequestId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 9. APPROVAL WORKFLOW & RELATIONSHIP-BASED RBAC
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 9.1 Line Manager: Inspect Pending Approvals
### Shows only leave requests routed to caller via active direct reporting line
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/leave/requests/pending-approvals
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}

### 9.2 Relationship-based RBAC: Unassigned Manager Attempts Approval (Expect HTTP 403 Forbidden)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/leave/requests/{{leaveRequestId}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{otherManagerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "comments": "Unauthorized approval attempt"
}

### 9.3 Assigned Line Manager Approves Leave Request
### Atomic update: pending_days decrements, used_days increments, DEDUCTION transaction written
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/leave/requests/{{leaveRequestId}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "comments": "Approved. Enjoy your time off!"
}

### 9.4 State Machine Conflict: Attempt Duplicate Approval on Terminal State (Expect HTTP 409 Conflict)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/leave/requests/{{leaveRequestId}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "comments": "Duplicate approval attempt"
}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 10. REJECTION & SELF-SERVICE CANCELLATION
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 10.1 Employee Submits a Second Leave Request
# @name submitSecondRequest
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/leave/requests
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "leaveTypeId": "{{listLeaveTypes.response.body.data[0].id}}",
    "startDate": "2026-10-12",
    "endDate": "2026-10-13",
    "reason": "Personal errands"
}

@secondRequestId = {{submitSecondRequest.response.body.data.id}}

### 10.2 Line Manager Rejects Request
### Pending hold released back to 0.00; used_days untouched
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/leave/requests/{{secondRequestId}}/reject
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "comments": "Cannot approve due to critical sprint release"
}

### 10.3 Employee Submits a Third Leave Request
# @name submitThirdRequest
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/leave/requests
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "leaveTypeId": "{{listLeaveTypes.response.body.data[0].id}}",
    "startDate": "2026-10-19",
    "endDate": "2026-10-20",
    "reason": "Doctor appointment"
}

@thirdRequestId = {{submitThirdRequest.response.body.data.id}}

### 10.4 Employee Cancels Own Pending Request
### Pending hold released back to 0.00; status transitions to CANCELLED
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/leave/requests/{{thirdRequestId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}

### 10.5 HR Admin Override Approval (Audited on behalf of absent manager)
# @name submitFourthRequest
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/leave/requests
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "leaveTypeId": "{{listLeaveTypes.response.body.data[0].id}}",
    "startDate": "2026-10-26",
    "endDate": "2026-10-27",
    "reason": "Emergency leave"
}

@fourthRequestId = {{submitFourthRequest.response.body.data.id}}

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/leave/requests/{{fourthRequestId}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "comments": "Approved by HR Admin on behalf of absent manager"
}

### ==============================================================================
### PHASE 5: HELP DESK TAXONOMY (Categories, Queues & SLA Policies)
### ==============================================================================

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 11. TICKET CATEGORIES
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 11.1 List All Active Categories (Authenticated)
# @name listCategories
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/helpdesk/categories
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}

### 11.2 Create Category (HR Admin only)
# @name createCategory
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/helpdesk/categories
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Cloud Infrastructure & DevOps",
    "code": "CLOUD_INFRA",
    "description": "AWS, GCP, Kubernetes, CI/CD pipeline issues and environment requests",
    "defaultPriority": "HIGH"
}

### Store Custom Category ID
@cloudCategoryId = {{createCategory.response.body.data.id}}

### 11.3 Employee Attempts Category Creation (Expect HTTP 403 Forbidden)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/helpdesk/categories
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Hacker Category",
    "code": "HACKER_CAT"
}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 12. SUPPORT QUEUES & MEMBERSHIP
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 12.1 List All Active Queues (Authenticated)
# @name listQueues
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/helpdesk/queues
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}

### 12.2 Create Support Queue (HR Admin only)
# @name createQueue
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/helpdesk/queues
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "DevOps & Cloud Reliability",
    "description": "Cloud infrastructure incident response and platform reliability team",
    "emailAlias": "devops-support@company.com"
}

### Store Queue ID
@devopsQueueId = {{createQueue.response.body.data.id}}

### 12.3 Add Support Agent to Queue (HR Admin only - sets assigned_by & assigned_at)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/helpdesk/queues/{{devopsQueueId}}/members
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "agentUserId": "{{adminUserId}}"
}

### 12.4 List Queue Members (Authenticated)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/helpdesk/queues/{{devopsQueueId}}/members
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 13. SLA POLICIES
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 13.1 List All Active SLA Policies (Authenticated)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/helpdesk/sla-policies
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}

### 13.2 Create SLA Policy with Escalation Contract (HR Admin only)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/helpdesk/sla-policies
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Executive VIP SLA",
    "priority": "URGENT",
    "firstResponseTargetMinutes": 10,
    "resolutionTargetMinutes": 60,
    "escalationRule": {
        "warnAtPercent": 70,
        "escalateToRole": "SUPPORT_LEAD",
        "notifyChannels": ["EMAIL", "SMS", "SLACK"]
    }
}


